# Published-release immutability manifest for Boot Bitch.
#
# Every non-comment line is "<sha256>  <path>" relative to this
# directory; each path is a byte-for-byte frozen copy of a published
# release artifact. Tests compare the live tree against these bytes;
# a mismatch means a published release was rewritten. Published
# releases are immutable (Development/docs/publishing.md): restore the frozen
# bytes and put the new work in the next version section instead.
#
# Rebaselined 2026-09-20: the maintainer approved a one-time concision pass
# over every release section (0.2.15-0.2.25) and authorized regenerating
# these frozen copies and manifest.sha256 from the rewritten live content.
# From this baseline the rewritten sections are frozen again; the exception
# must not be reused. See Development/docs/publishing.md (Release invariants).
#
# Lead-simplification rebaseline 2026-09-20 (follow-up): the release lead
# sentences were simplified under the same one-time approval (no
# previous-release wording, short change summaries) and the changed README
# and CHANGELOG sections, release notes and captures were regenerated from
# the rewritten live content; the leads are frozen from this baseline.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-19 from the canonical tree (the content published on
# GitHub main) and cross-checked against the staging clone tags.
# Provenance notes:
#   - 0.2.15-0.2.17, 0.2.23 README/CHANGELOG sections: identical to
#     the matching git tag in ~/Projects/Boot_Bitch-github.
#   - 0.2.18, 0.2.19, 0.2.20 README sections: frozen from the published
#     docs. The tag snapshots carry pre-restoration text and differ;
#     commit 134919b restored the sections on main on 2026-09-14.
#   - 0.2.21, 0.2.22: no git tags exist for these published releases;
#     frozen from the published docs.
#   - 0.2.24 README section and docs/release-notes-0.2.24.md: frozen
#     from the published docs. Tag v0.2.24 carries the pre-correction
#     cumulative text; commit d2bf12b scoped it to 0.2.23...0.2.24 on
#     2026-09-18 (already on main).
#   - docs/release-notes-0.2.15.md through 0.2.19.md: never published
#     as separate files; no fixture.
#   - captures/release-<v>/ mirrors the untracked Development/release-<v>/
#     release workspace (not tracked in git and excluded from mirror
#     syncs). The "captures/" name avoids the sync's "Development/"
#     exclude dropping the frozen copies. They are checked only when
#     Development/release-<v>/ exists.
#
